    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Category definitions and precedence",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 15
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every organization appears once. Evaluation order:\n\n1. **missing_billing_account** \u2014 no billing row.\n2. **unknown** \u2014 unknown billing class/status, blank subscription ID, or only one of subscription ID/status present.\n3. **subscribed** \u2014 stored status `active`, even if cancellation is scheduled. No receipt or invoice verification.\n4. **sponsored / grandfathered** \u2014 matching billing class, after the checks above; exemptions take precedence over trial/inactive status.\n5. **trial** \u2014 standard, `trialing`, deadline in the future. Deadline is period end, falling back to redeemed-at + campaign days for a redeemed trial. Unknown if neither exists.\n6. **expired_past_due** \u2014 standard with elapsed trial (deadline inclusive), `past_due`, `unpaid`, `canceled`, `paused`, or `incomplete_expired`.\n7. **incomplete** \u2014 standard, checkout subscription is `incomplete`.\n8. **no_subscription** \u2014 standard, billing row exists with both subscription ID and status absent. A customer ID alone does not imply a subscription.\n\nTrial reservations alone do not prove a trial. Historical snapshots reflect recorded billing state, not revenue or human engagement."
      }
    },
